# Sonde evidence-backed explanations implementation plan

## Phase 0 — adjudicate the existing orientation maps

- [ ] MAP-GATE-1: Run the frozen cold comparison of both architecture maps
  Read `probes/visual-map/PROTOCOL.md` and, without inspecting source or using `sonde query` first, answer Q1–Q4 and C1 from the complete map and Markdown in the required counterbalanced order, then answer Q5–Q6 from the simple map and Markdown. Record each raw answer, elapsed time, and confidence stated before checking in `probes/visual-map/RAW-RESULTS.md`; identify the map builder and answerer so the separation-of-roles and C1 void conditions are auditable. Do not change `src/map/`, either generated artifact, the protocol, or any threshold. Verify every required cell is populated and C1 was not used as a map task. Change nothing else.

- [ ] MAP-GATE-2: Adjudicate the map experiment and record independent verdicts
  Using `sonde query` and the indexed graph only after MAP-GATE-1 is frozen, adjudicate Q1–Q6 and C1, verify the dense-graph, dirty/freshness, heuristic-only Swift↔TypeScript pair, and MCP-only walkthrough cases from protocol §4.1, and write `probes/visual-map/RESULTS.md`. Apply the complete and simple map formulas separately as `PASS`, `MARGINAL`, `FAIL`, or `VOID`, include the evidence for every score, and record a Whyline decision; a `MARGINAL` must stop for an explicit human decision and must not authorize later map work. Run `nvm use && npm test -- tests/map tests/cli/map.test.ts` to ensure adjudication did not alter behavior. Change nothing else.

## Phase 1 — expose only validated orientation surfaces

- [ ] ORIENT-1: Verify sonde doc discoverability independently of the map gate
  Audit `README.md`, CLI help, and `sonde init` so the already-supported `sonde doc` workflow is present in the command inventory and init guidance without changing graph or document semantics. Add or update CLI documentation tests, pack and install the tarball into an empty temporary project, and verify successful `sonde doc`, `--check`, dirty/drift provenance, missing-index guidance, and missing-toolchain/parse warnings by reading the output. This task is authorized regardless of either map verdict and must not advertise `sonde map`. Change nothing else.

- [ ] MAP-GATE-3: Apply the recorded map verdict without changing graph semantics
  Read `probes/visual-map/RESULTS.md`. For each `PASS`, document only that retained view in `README.md` and `sonde init` guidance, naming the exact protocol questions it improved, and clean-install verify its normal plus dirty/degraded output; for each `FAIL`, leave it unadvertised as research code unless the human verdict explicitly says to remove it; for `MARGINAL` or `VOID`, stop without modifying map code or docs. Update the stable map rule in `AGENTS.md` in the same change if the human disposition changes which view is retained. Do not add an orientation preface to `ARCHITECTURE.md`, change projection semantics, or touch focused explanations. Change nothing else.

## Phase 2 — freeze and run the focused Markdown experiment

- [ ] FOCUS-1: Freeze the focused-explanation evaluation protocol
  Create `probes/focused-explanation/PROTOCOL.md` before building packet code. Pin Sonde plus at least one unfamiliar permissively licensed repository and revision; define at least two flow questions, two impact questions including a working-tree diff, one identifier-poor question, and one exact direct-lookup control; compare file-tree/grep/read, the current three Sonde tools, and a pre-seeded Markdown packet. Fix the counterbalancing, participant/session isolation, correctness rubric, elapsed-time/tool-call/read/context-byte or estimated-token/confidence/uncertainty fields, projection-specific PASS rule from spec §8, and `MARGINAL`/`FAIL` stop behavior. Verify the task inventory and every metric mechanically, and do not implement a packet or inspect answers in this task. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FOCUS-2: Commit the reviewed answer key separately from the protocol
  Create `probes/focused-explanation/ANSWER-KEY.md` in a separate task/commit after FOCUS-1. For every pinned question, resolve the packet seed in advance, cite reviewed source and graph evidence, list required and acceptable evidence, static-analysis caveats, expected direct-lookup result, and the exact working-tree diff fixture; ambiguous identifier-poor wording must retain its ambiguity rather than invent a seed. Have the answer key reviewed against the pinned revisions and add a script or test that rejects missing questions, seeds, evidence citations, or revision hashes. Do not change the frozen protocol or production `src/`. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FOCUS-3: Build probe-local evidence ordering and seed resolution
  Under `probes/focused-explanation/`, add probe-only types and database readers that resolve a stable key, then a unique qualified name, then a unique short name, returning bounded candidates instead of choosing an ambiguous seed. Implement the spec §4 total edge comparator exactly: tier, descending existing `score()` with `pathFocusMatch: false`, HEURISTIC-only confidence, source key, destination key, relationship kind, numbered site before missing site, then edge id; collapse duplicate source/destination/kind rows while retaining all distinct sites in that order. Add focused tests proving tier always beats score, confidence cannot reorder resolved edges, scoring uses reached-node depth, and duplicate representative/site behavior. Export nothing from `src/` and change no production API. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FOCUS-4: Generate throwaway static-flow Markdown packets
  Add the probe flow projection and renderer under `probes/focused-explanation/`, reusing existing rank, store, freshness, and repository-boundary seams. Cover forest BFS with one parent, depth-first root-to-node path numbering, self/ancestor cycles, shared diamonds, equal-shortest predecessor-DAG `--to` paths, duplicate CALLS/REFERENCES sites, non-recursive possible HEURISTIC links, one-hop reverse IMPLEMENTS/INHERITS fan-out, external/unresolved caveats, direct seed-only TESTS lookup, bounds, and deterministic next-file selection. Render the exact marker, headings, static-reachability disclaimer, evidence tables, shortfall sentences, and no generation timestamp; add golden tests for cycles, shared paths, no path, truncation, zero/one/two next files, and unavailable test evidence. Keep all code probe-local. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FOCUS-5: Generate throwaway change-impact Markdown packets
  Add the probe impact projection and renderer under `probes/focused-explanation/`, adapting the existing all-tier reverse BFS rather than flow semantics. Resolve explicit seeds or map a pinned working-tree diff's changed ranges to current indexed symbols; keep COMPILER, LEXICAL, and HEURISTIC rows together in ascending depth groups ordered by the shared comparator; treat IMPLEMENTS/INHERITS as ordinary impact edges; perform one direct seed-scoped incoming TESTS lookup; preserve freshness, token-budget, omission, unresolved, parse/toolchain, and bound disclosures. Golden-test multiple seeds, ambiguous/missing seeds, unavailable Git, no mapped diff symbols, all-tier ordering, token truncation, and the required “may affect”/coverage wording. Keep all code probe-local. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FOCUS-6: Run all three experimental conditions and preserve raw observations
  Execute the frozen protocol in isolated fresh sessions for both pinned repositories and record condition order, answers, correctness pending adjudication, elapsed time, reads/tool calls, context bytes or estimated tokens, stated confidence, and recognition of uncertainty/static limits in `probes/focused-explanation/RAW-RESULTS.md`. In the packet condition, use only the pre-committed seed from the answer key; in the other conditions, do not expose that seed. Save generated packets and machine-readable measurements under the probe, redact no unfavorable result, and run the protocol validator. Do not revise thresholds, answer keys, packet algorithms, or production code after seeing results. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FOCUS-7: Adjudicate flow and impact as independent product gates
  Compare FOCUS-6 against `ANSWER-KEY.md`, record correctness and direct-control behavior, and write `probes/focused-explanation/VERDICT.md` with separate `PASS`, `MARGINAL`, or `FAIL` decisions for flow and impact. A projection passes only when it improves at least two appropriate comprehension tasks without reducing control correctness; do not fabricate percentage or timing thresholds from a single participant. Record the Whyline decision and the exact production tasks authorized; on `MARGINAL`, stop for a human decision, and on `FAIL`, explicitly end investment in that projection while leaving its probe evidence intact. Verify the raw record is immutable relative to its pre-adjudication commit. Change nothing else.

## Phase 3 — productize only projections authorized by FOCUS-7

- [ ] EXPLAIN-1: Add strict explanation request parsing and symbol resolution
  Proceed only if `probes/focused-explanation/VERDICT.md` records at least one projection `PASS`. Add internal request/bounds/error types and a reusable resolver under `src/explain/` that accepts stable key, unique qualified name, then unique short name; missing names must include the attempted identifier and a `sonde search` suggestion, while ambiguity must return bounded candidate stable keys and never score-select one. Validate defaults of depth 3/nodes 100/time 2 seconds, reject non-positive values and values above depth 6/nodes 500, require exactly symbols or `--from-git-diff` for impact, and keep `--question` as metadata only. Add failing-first unit tests for every resolution and validation branch. Do not introduce a public schema, JSON mode, HTML, or a fourth MCP tool. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-2: Add explanation-specific indexed-evidence readers and the shared comparator
  Add narrow `Store`/`src/explain/` read APIs that return symbol locations/ranges, edge ids, tiers, confidence, site lines, fan-in/exported inputs, external/unresolved rows, indexed-at provenance, and compiler/pyright provenance without exposing raw SQL to renderers. Implement the one total comparator from spec §4 and duplicate-edge representative/site aggregation once for every projection. Tests must prove `COMPILER > LEXICAL > HEURISTIC`, score uses the candidate's displayed depth with `pathFocusMatch: false`, confidence is consulted only for HEURISTIC ties, missing lines sort last, edge id is the final tie-breaker, and all sites survive collapse. Do not alter existing `query_graph` or impact ordering yet. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-3: Assemble truthful evidence state and shared node allowances
  Add an internal explanation context builder that calls `ensureFresh`, reports root hash, revision, nullable dirty state, stable index time, freshness/drift, parse failures, compiler/pyright provenance, warnings, and remaining depth/node/time/token allowances. Preserve partial results for drift, parse, missing toolchain, and truncation, but turn no index and schema mismatch into typed non-zero errors with exact rebuild commands; include no volatile generation timestamp in stdout semantics. Unit-test fresh, inline-refreshed, dirty, over-drift, parse-failure, missing-toolchain, no-index, and schema-mismatch states without executing repository code. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FLOW-1: Implement deterministic resolved forest traversal
  Proceed only if flow is authorized. Add `src/explain/flow.ts` forest mode over outgoing resolved CALLS plus non-duplicate REFERENCES. Run level-order BFS with the seed pre-discovered, sort the whole frontier with the shared comparator, retain one parent per destination, then emit one complete root-to-node path per accepted tree edge depth-first with comparator-ordered siblings and numbered first appearances; record self/ancestor edges as cycles and other rediscovery as shared nodes without enqueueing either. Enforce request depth/node/time bounds while building and expose exact bound/omission state. Add tests for sibling ordering, self-loop, ancestor cycle, diamond sharing, duplicate call/reference sites, exact-fit bounds, and deterministic prefixes. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FLOW-2: Implement every bounded equal-shortest targeted path
  Proceed only if flow is authorized. Add `--to` traversal with a distance map and comparator-ordered predecessor lists: finish the entire predecessor frontier when the target first appears, retain every equal-distance predecessor, discard longer arrivals, and reconstruct simple paths depth-first through the increasing-distance DAG. Mark repeated symbols `shared with path N`, never cycle; return success with the exact no-indexed-path wording when unreachable; under bounds emit the deterministic fitting prefix and known omitted-path count. Test alternate equal parents, cycles and longer detours, target-at-seed, unreachable targets with unresolved evidence, node/time truncation, and stable path numbering. Change nothing else.

- [ ] FLOW-3: Add possible links, implementation fan-out, and scoped caveats
  Proceed only if flow is authorized. For the seed and resolved primary-path nodes only, add one non-recursive outgoing HEURISTIC CALLS/REFERENCES lookup and at most one reverse IMPLEMENTS/INHERITS hop, ordered by the shared comparator and scored at owner depth plus one; never add these rows to BFS parents/predecessors or bridge a missing segment. Aggregate scoped external/unresolved counts and named reasons, consume only the remaining semantic-node allowance, and label every inferred implementer “implementation fan-out.” Tests must prove auxiliary rows cannot extend paths, heuristic calls remain possible links, fan-out direction is correct, and caps disclose rather than silently drop evidence. Change nothing else.

- [ ] IMPACT-1: Map working-tree diff hunks to current symbols with hard Git errors
  Proceed only if impact is authorized. Extend `src/repo/git.ts` through `RepoBoundary`-safe inputs to parse the current tracked working-tree diff's zero-context changed ranges, then select indexed symbols whose current ranges overlap those hunks; list added/modified files or hunks that map to no symbol as omissions rather than guessing, and treat unavailable Git state as a typed non-zero error instead of an empty diff. Keep explicit symbols mutually exclusive with diff mode. Add tests for staged plus unstaged edits, multiple hunks, additions, deleted/unmappable files, non-Git roots, command failure, and paths containing spaces. Change nothing else.

- [ ] IMPACT-2: Adapt reverse impact traversal to the explanation contract
  Proceed only if impact is authorized. Refactor or wrap `getImpactRadius` so request-specific lower bounds, remaining node/time allowance, resolved seed reasons, direct dependants, and transitive depth groups are returned while preserving all-tier reverse CALLS/REFERENCES/IMPLEMENTS/INHERITS semantics. Order every frontier by the shared comparator without splitting HEURISTIC rows, preserve freshness and existing token-budget estimation/omission disclosure, and never use “will break” or “blast radius.” Add regression tests for cycles, multiple seeds, every edge kind, cross-tier order, exact-fit and each bound, diff-derived seeds, and unchanged existing MCP behavior. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-4: Add one seed-scoped structural-test lookup for both projections
  Add a shared incoming TESTS reader invoked once after seed resolution: flow uses only its source seed, never `--to` or path nodes; impact uses its explicit or diff-derived seed set. Deduplicate test symbols/files, order retained edges with the total comparator, consume the request's remaining node allowance, never enter either primary traversal, and always label rows HEURISTIC with the coverage caveat. When no producer/evidence exists, render the identical unavailable-evidence sentence rather than infer tests from filenames or claim none exist. Test injected TESTS rows, duplicate seeds/files, remaining-cap truncation, flow-target exclusion, and the unavailable case. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-5: Select exactly two evidence-backed next source files
  Add a pure selector implementing spec §6's candidate sequence: distinct non-test seed files by stable key; primary symbols by depth, tier, score, stable key, path; then flow-only fan-out and possible-link files in the same order. Keep the earliest qualifying position, exclude TESTS/unresolved/external/parse-failure/filename guesses, and include a targeted flow destination only when a displayed resolved path reached it. Test duplicate paths, multiple impact seeds, reached/unreached targets, auxiliary-only files, and the exact one-file and zero-file shortfall sentences. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-6: Render deterministic projection-specific Markdown
  Add a pure Markdown renderer with the exact ownership marker and H1, fixed H2 order, fixed Request and Evidence-state field order, compact answer, flow `Static structural paths` or impact `Impact by depth`, Read next, flow-only auxiliary section, structural tests, and limits/warnings. Every topology row must show stable keys, relationship kind, tier, repository-relative source location and recorded line; include the exact static-reachability disclaimer, coverage caveat, unresolved/external/truncation/parse/toolchain disclosures, and no volatile generation receipt on stdout. Escape repository and user text as untrusted Markdown. Golden-test both projections, dirty/partial states, no path, all bounds, all next-file cardinalities, hostile Markdown/HTML strings, and byte identity on repeated renders. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-7: Add atomic Sonde-owned repository file replacement
  Extend `RepoBoundary` with a focused generated-artifact writer used by explanations: validate repository-relative destination and links, re-check the real parent to defeat symlink-parent escapes, require the exact ownership marker before overwrite, render/validate fully before opening, create a known sibling temporary file, write and flush it, close it, atomically rename it, and remove only that known temp on failure while preserving the prior good artifact. Add fault-injection tests for traversal, absolute paths, symlink files and parents, unmarked destinations, write/flush/close/rename failures, successful create/replace, and temp cleanup. Do not retrofit unrelated artifacts in this task. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-8: Wire the passing projection commands into the CLI
  Add a Commander `sonde explain` family only for projections authorized by FOCUS-7, using the exact spec §3 arguments and options. Default to Markdown on stdout; write only an explicit repository-relative `--out`; canonicalize the displayed generation command; return zero for truthful no-path, degraded, and truncated packets, and non-zero before writing for invalid/ambiguous/missing seeds, unavailable Git, no index/schema mismatch, unsafe paths, or refused overwrite. Reject implicit or combined impact seed modes and do not add `--json`, HTML, timestamps, model prose, or MCP tools. Add CLI tests for help/argument parsing, stdout purity, question metadata having no topology effect, output ownership, every exit-status class, and both passing projections' representative happy paths. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-9: Lock end-to-end semantics with multilingual and security fixtures
  Add end-to-end golden fixtures exercising TypeScript and at least one other shipped adapter, compiler/lexical/heuristic evidence, ambiguous names, equal paths, cycles, implementation fan-out, diff impact, parse degradation, unresolved/external refs, and absent TESTS production. Verify every rendered topology fact exists in SQLite, no heuristic is promoted or traversed as resolved flow, all repository reads/writes go through `RepoBoundary`, hostile repository strings cannot inject Markdown/HTML, wall-clock truncation is truthful but excluded from byte-golden equality, and `npm run typecheck && npm test` pass under `nvm use`. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-10: Document and clean-install verify the supported explanation surface
  Update `README.md`, CLI inventory, and `sonde init` hint with only projections that passed, the intent-routing table, static-not-runtime language, bounds, ambiguity behavior, stdout/`--out`, `.sonde/` gitignore recommendation, TESTS caveat, and corrective error commands; do not advertise failed projections, maps lacking their gate, JSON, HTML, or model prose. Pack the package, install it into an empty temporary directory, build throwaway TypeScript and non-TypeScript repositories, read successful and degraded output, and verify both the presence and absence of warnings in the appropriate cases. Record the commands and observed semantic output in `docs/explain-clean-install-verification.md`. Change nothing else.

- [ ] EXPLAIN-11: Release the validated explanation CLI
  relay-profile: release
  Only after EXPLAIN-9 and EXPLAIN-10 pass, update `package.json`, both version fields in `server.json`, `CHANGELOG.md`, and release notes for exactly the supported projection set. Run typecheck/tests and repeat the clean install from the packed artifact, then run npm publish, GitHub tag/release, and MCP Registry publish as separate commands with authentication checked before each; query all three registries afterward and require the new MCP version to report `isLatest: true`. Do not publish a skill, optional sink, or unpassed projection in this release. Change nothing else.

## Phase 4 — evaluate routing guidance after the CLI ships

- [ ] SKILL-GATE-1: Freeze the fresh-session routing evaluation
  After at least one explanation projection is released, create `probes/sonde-explain-skill/PROTOCOL.md` with fresh-session tasks spanning vague discovery, direct relationships, edit impact, repository orientation, shipped flow, ambiguity, non-code diagrams, and legitimate grep. Compare sessions with and without the skill; freeze correct route selection, exploratory reads/tool calls, ambiguity handling, and the qualitative gate before writing skill instructions. Do not count “zero grep” as success and do not modify CLI/MCP code. Change nothing else.

- [ ] SKILL-GATE-2: Prototype the thin sonde-explain skill locally
  Create the probe skill with routing and usage guidance only: vague discovery→`find_symbols`, direct relationship→`query_graph`, edit safety→impact, orientation→`sonde doc` plus only retained map views, feature flow→a shipped flow command, ambiguity→ask for a symbol/file, and non-code topology→state Sonde lacks evidence and stop. Return compact Markdown to agents and only a path/launch instruction for human HTML; never place HTML/SVG in context or let instructions add/remove/retarget/promote topology. Validate the skill structure and examples without publishing it. Change nothing else.

- [ ] SKILL-GATE-3: Run fresh sessions and decide whether the skill earns publication
  Execute SKILL-GATE-1 with isolated sessions, preserve raw transcripts/measurements, and write `probes/sonde-explain-skill/VERDICT.md` comparing correct Sonde route selection and exploratory reads. Record a Whyline decision: `PASS` authorizes a separate skills-repository release, `MARGINAL` stops for a human, and `FAIL` retains only the research artifact. Do not revise the protocol or runtime to rescue a result. Change nothing else.

- [ ] SKILL-GATE-4: Publish the passing skill from a separate repository
  relay-profile: release
  Only on `PASS`, create or use a dedicated `sonde-explain-skill` repository under the same owner as Sonde, copy the validated thin skill without bundling Sonde runtime code, add installation/version/release metadata, and run its own validation and fresh install. Tag and publish from that repository, then add only a link and compatibility note to Sonde; never publish the skill from the Sonde npm package or change the three-tool MCP surface. Change nothing else.

## Phase 5 — add no optional surface without a measured residual gap

- [ ] MCP-GATE-1: Measure shell-less access through the current three tools
  Freeze a small protocol under `probes/explanation-mcp/` for a documented shell-less client to obtain the already-winning explanation semantics using `find_symbols`, `query_graph`, and `get_impact_radius`; record correctness, calls, context, bounds, and missing semantic fields, then run it without changing schemas. Write a verdict that either closes the gap with no code or identifies the minimum unavailable fields; a desire for convenience alone does not pass. Change nothing else.

- [ ] MCP-GATE-2: Add bounded paths_from only if the shell-less gate proves it necessary
  Proceed only if MCP-GATE-1 records a concrete supported-workflow failure. Extend the existing `query_graph` schema and implementation with `paths_from` accepting one stable seed, optional stable target, depth, nodes, and token budget; return semantic nodes and tiered links in the existing response envelope with no repository writes, HTML/SVG/layout, free-form seed guessing, or fourth tool. Reuse the production comparator/traversal, preserve all bounds/warnings, test MCP schema compatibility and token truncation, and repeat the shell-less protocol to confirm the measured gap closes. Change nothing else.

- [ ] SINK-GATE-1: Test a disposable second presentation without creating a product contract
  For a passing projection only, render a probe-local HTML view from the identical semantic packet and run a frozen human comparison against Markdown; preserve raw results and require a comprehension improvement, not visual preference. If it fails or is marginal, stop and keep Markdown as the sole sink; do not add a format flag or production schema. Change nothing else.

- [ ] SINK-GATE-2: Introduce an internal envelope only after a second sink passes
  Proceed only on a recorded SINK-GATE-1 `PASS`. Add a non-exported `ExplanationEnvelope` containing exactly the semantic fields in spec §7, move database access out of both renderers, keep layout coordinates/styles out of the envelope, and add semantic-equivalence tests after stripping presentation-only data; the HTML view must retain text evidence cues so color is never the sole tier signal. Add the smallest reviewed CLI exposure for the winning sink, keep Markdown default, and do not call the type a public IR or add JSON without a demonstrated agent consumer. Change nothing else.

